[{"id": "HO-N2_dung-nham-ve__4", "prompt": "Create an image. IMPORTANT LAYOUT: exactly 4 columns x 3 rows of equal cells, landscape 4:3 canvas. PIXEL ART game VFX sprite sheet (crisp visible pixels, limited palette, dark 1-2px outline, like a 16-bit console game), 12 animation frames read left to right, top to bottom: the LEGENDARY ultimate skill of Dung Nham Vệ, a fire creature. Flat solid magenta background #FF00FF everywhere. CUTOUT RULE: every frame is ONE isolated effect shape floating on magenta, with magenta clearly visible all around it (about 6% gap to each cell border); NEVER fill a cell with a rectangle of fire, smoke, water, sky or ground; no background scenery, no creature body, no text, no numbers, no grid lines, no borders. Make each effect as BIG as possible inside that gap: a huge, heavy, screen-shaking legendary move. Frames: Ultimate, 4x3 grid, plays once. Row 1 (frames 1-4): 1 = tall white spiky flame burst with rocks on the ground, 2 = round fiery explosion cloud with rocks flying, 3 = narrower burst with rocks and flame, 4 = big brown smoke clouds with sparks over cracked ground. Row 2 (frames 5-8, seamless loop): a round, cute lava-rock creature (spiky dark cracked shell with red glowing cracks, a spiral mark on forehead, glowing yellow eyes, stubby stone feet) rolling/charging right with flame streaks trailing behind it. Row 3 (frames 9-12): 9 = the creature glowing bright orange and about to burst, 10 = white explosion with big lava rocks flying around, 11 = rocks and curling flame arcs, 12 = smoke cloud above small rubble and cracked ground. Row 3 (frames 9-12) REPLACES the description above for that row: a LINGERING SLOW FIELD, seamless loop, 3/4 top view: a very wide flat oval almost as wide as the cell, molten lava ground with a ring of low flames around its edge, slow drifting embers and heat haze, engraved with a glowing golden rune circle and glyph ring, small golden lightning sparks crackling on it, reading clearly as a zone that SLOWS enemies standing in it; the runes pulse and the particles drift between frames. LEGENDARY look: divine and spectacular like an anime boss final super move: thick jagged golden-white lightning bolts forking around the effect in every frame (a different bolt shape each frame so it flickers), roaring red-orange fire with white-gold cores trailing in the direction of motion, a celestial phoenix-fire motif, white-gold sun flames, shockwave rings and light rays on the big moments. Colours red, orange, yellow plus radiant gold."}, {"id": "HO-N2_dung-nham-ve__aura", "prompt": "Create an image. IMPORTANT LAYOUT: exactly 4 columns x 2 rows of equal cells, wide landscape 2:1 canvas. PIXEL ART game VFX sprite sheet (crisp visible pixels, limited palette, dark 1-2px outline, like a 16-bit console game), 8 animation frames read left to right, top to bottom: the LEGENDARY power-up aura (row 1 a ring drawn behind the creature with an empty middle, row 2 its spirit beast shown above its head) of Dung Nham Vệ, a fire creature. Flat solid magenta background #FF00FF everywhere. CUTOUT RULE: every frame is ONE isolated effect shape floating on magenta, with magenta clearly visible all around it (about 6% gap to each cell border); NEVER fill a cell with a rectangle of fire, smoke, water, sky or ground; no background scenery, no creature body, no text, no numbers, no grid lines, no borders. Make each effect as BIG as possible inside that gap: a huge, heavy, screen-shaking legendary move. Frames: Row 1 (frames 1-4, seamless loop): an upright ring of fire with many cracked lava boulders orbiting in it, hollow centre, and a flat ring of rocks forming a ground platform at the bottom; drawn behind the creature, rocks and flames shift each frame. Row 2 (frames 5-8, spirit beast above head): 5 = swirling vortex of flame and rocks, 6 = vortex forms a rock-armoured lava eagle/dragon head facing right with crest of rocks and open beak, 7 = head opens its toothed mouth breathing a bright fire blast to the right, 8 = dissolves into diagonal streaming rocks and flame. LEGENDARY look: divine and spectacular like an anime boss final super move: thick jagged golden-white lightning bolts forking around the effect in every frame (a different bolt shape each frame so it flickers), roaring red-orange fire with white-gold cores trailing in the direction of motion, a celestial phoenix-fire motif, white-gold sun flames, shockwave rings and light rays on the big moments. Colours red, orange, yellow plus radiant gold."}, {"id": "HO-N2_dung-nham-ve__2", "prompt": "Create an image. IMPORTANT LAYOUT: exactly 4 columns x 2 rows of equal cells, wide landscape 2:1 canvas. PIXEL ART game VFX sprite sheet (crisp visible pixels, limited palette, dark 1-2px outline, like a 16-bit console game), 8 animation frames read left to right, top to bottom: the LEGENDARY main skill of Dung Nham Vệ, a fire creature. Flat solid magenta background #FF00FF everywhere. CUTOUT RULE: every frame is ONE isolated effect shape floating on magenta, with magenta clearly visible all around it (about 6% gap to each cell border) (except a horizontal beam segment meant to tile, which touches the left and right cell edges); NEVER fill a cell with a rectangle of fire, smoke, water, sky or ground; no background scenery, no creature body, no text, no numbers, no grid lines, no borders. Make each effect as BIG as possible inside that gap: a huge, heavy, screen-shaking legendary move. Frames: Row 1 (frames 1-4, plays once): a flat oval patch of ground covered by molten lava rocks and flames with glowing cracks; flames on top die down each frame until frame 4 is mostly cooled brown cracked rock with thin glowing seams. Row 2 (frames 5-8, seamless loop): a hollow ring of curved flame blades spinning around an empty oval centre, with tan dust puffs and small rocks orbiting; ring rotates each frame. LEGENDARY look: divine and spectacular like an anime boss final super move: thick jagged golden-white lightning bolts 